@startuml
title Incident Desk UML Architecture Diagram

allowmixing
!pragma layout smetana

top to bottom direction

skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam nodesep 65
skinparam ranksep 70
skinparam ArrowColor #333333
skinparam ClassBorderColor #555555
skinparam ClassFontColor #111111

hide methods
hide stereotypes
hide circle

actor User

class "Startup / composition" as Startup #F2F2F2 {
    IncidentDeskApplication
    ApplicationContext
}

class "Presentation (JavaFX)" as UI #E8F4E8 {
    ApplicationNavigator
    DefaultViewFactory
    ReporterPage / ResponderPage
    Administrator pages
}

class "Application use cases" as UseCases #E5F1FB {
    SessionService
    IncidentService
    AttachmentService
    Account / audit / SLO services
}

class "Domain" as Domain #FFF7DC {
    Incident / Account
    IncidentLifecycle
    SloCalculator
}

class "Persistence interfaces" as Ports #EDF2FF {
    IncidentStore
    AccountRepository
    AuditRepository / AttachmentStore
}

class "Local-file adapters" as Storage #F9E5EE {
    LocalApplicationStore
    RecoverySafeFile
    AttachmentFiles
}

database "application data directory\nincident-desk.dat / .bak\nattachments/ + lock" as DataFile #FFFFFF

User -down-> UI : interacts with\nrole views
Startup -down-> UI : constructs navigator\nand view factory
Startup -right-> UseCases : assembles shared\nservices
UI -right-> UseCases : invokes use cases
UseCases -down-> Domain : applies lifecycle\nand domain rules
UseCases -right-> Ports : calls interfaces\nfor durable state
Storage ..up|> Ports : implements
Storage -right-> DataFile : reads and safely\nreplaces local data

note bottom of Ports
The application layer uses interfaces;
ApplicationContext wires in LocalApplicationStore.
end note

@enduml
